# Asymptote rules for coding agents
- Light theme only. Use only the tokens in DESIGN.md. No dark surfaces, no shadows, no new colors or fonts.
- Amber is only for hint actions. Emerald is only for progress and success.
- Sentence case labels. No emoji, no uppercase micro-labels, no jargon.
- Never show guessed content. Hints, solutions and complexity appear only for verified problems; otherwise show "No verified hints yet".
- Language lists come from LeetCode's langSlug data for each problem, never hardcoded.
- Never invent problem ids or slugs. Never save a problem whose real id cannot be resolved.
- Tests must not touch the network or tracker.db. Run npm run lint, npm test and npm run build before finishing.
- Do not push, rewrite git history or delete user data without asking.
